    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0509" n="439" xml:id="pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-17T14:00:00-06:00">February 17, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Referring to my telegram No. 14, February 16 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >15</hi>], 6 p.m. The Minister of Foreign Affairs told me yesterday with
                    reference to Izaguirre’s visit to Washington that Honduras is anxious that
                    forthcoming Conference shall accomplish something practical and really effective
                    in the interest of peace in Central America. He said that while he realized that
                    the United States did not wish to mix in purely Central American projects that
                    President Carias desires Izaguirre and Dr. Paz Baraona<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d520-f1"/> to consult with the Department regarding the moral
                    support that our Government may be able to extend in the interest of peace in
                    Central America. He did not suggest specifically what form of moral support his
                    Government desired but intimated that without some assurance of support from the
                    United States it would be very difficult to negotiate satisfactory modified
                    peace treaties at the forthcoming Conference at Guatemala City.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Central American missions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d520-f1" n="17" xml:id="d520-f1-content">
                <p>Miguel Paz Baraona, Honduran Minister in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
